# Defect 520, 2026-10-09, panel 201's R3, ratified: the witness that replaced
# `fixedbugs-508-a-self-call-through-a-function-value-aborts-at-every-level`
# once `check` refuses a self-call through a value bound once to the function
# (that case is in `check/` since). `go` returns when `n` is 0, a way out by
# syntax, so the rule lets it through; called with 1 it never takes it, and
# it calls itself through `f` until the stack is exhausted, an abort at every
# level (panel 199's R2). Under the sanitiser the runtime's guard yields to
# ASan, which says `stack-overflow`.
function go(n: i64) -> i64
    if n == 0
        return 0
    f = go
    return f(n)

function main()
    print(go(1))
